{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774722,"nonce":"gHvgDsOWzDL7qZdxxe0PBSV26xU=","title":"ADR-0056: Run Takes (version history) + attempt-grain evidence","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #41 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `feat/adr-0056-takes` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-19T20:31:17Z · Merged: 2026-07-20T04:59:22Z\n\nImplements **ADR-0056** (included in this PR): the run's version history and the end of silent evidence destruction.\n\n\nA **Take** is the span of a run between two human restarts — a derived lens over the event log, stored nowhere. The backend's job is to version **evidence at the attempt grain** (the fence unit `{run, step, attempt}` becomes the storage unit); the UI derives Takes client-side and replays the log for snapshot-at-boundary views.\n\n\n- **Three evidence-destruction bugs fixed**: `step_runs.results` / `output_snapshot` were latest-wins (a restart destroyed the prior attempt's data and left its CAS root dangling for the GC to sweep); `artifacts` was `(run_id, name)` + `ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE` — a retry silently overwrote the failed attempt's failure report, contradicting the migration's own \"immutable once written\" comment.\n- `attempts` gains `results` / `output_snapshot` / `consumed` (consumption provenance: which upstream attempt each attempt built on, stamped at launch); `step_runs` keeps the latest-evidence denorm, stamped with `evidence_attempt`. Failed attempts' artifacts are now harvested too; the bare name-addressed download resolves to the latest **successful** version, `?step=\u0026attempt=` pins an exact one.\n- **New events**: `RunRestartRequested {target, invalidated, by}` (the Take boundary + the who-restarted audit fact, emitted before any re-arming) and `AttemptReadopted` (a control plane resuming supervision of an attempt it didn't launch — the durability wedge made visible; previously invisible).\n- GC marks **every** attempt's snapshot live, not just each step's latest.\n- Reads: `?attempt=` on results/workspace, `GET …/consumed`, artifact list with provenance + `of_record`.\n\n\n- **Take dropdown** in the run header; a closed Take is a read-only snapshot-at-boundary replay (DAG, evidence, artifacts, Activity all as-of that instant), straddling steps show *running* with a \"finished in Take N →\" affordance; mutations disabled except debug-pod and \"New run\".\n- **Merged step pane** replaces the stacked Logs panel + Inspector: an attempt strip (cause-labeled chips — retry vs restart — failure class, re-adoption marker, dead-letter terminal) scopes Logs/Results/Outputs/Workspace to one `(step, attempt)`; Outputs shows recorded consumption (\"built on build@a3\").\n- **Restart vs Re-run untangled**: distinct icons/labels (\"Restart step — opens a new take\" vs \"New run\").\n\n\n- 440 tests green across 100 suites against real Postgres (new: boundary event + invalidation set + principal; exactly-one `AttemptReadopted` across a control-plane crash; attempt evidence survives reruns; consumption provenance; artifact version retention + of-record refusal to serve failed bytes).\n- **Live-verified** on the local stack (throwaway DB + MinIO, local executor, real browser): created a diamond run, restarted `build` while `docs` was mid-flight, confirmed the dropdown, banner, straddle affordance, frontier-pinned strip, and read-only gating. This pass caught two real bugs fixed in-branch: per-cycle Scheduler construction made every routine re-poll emit `AttemptReadopted` (fixed with a process-lifetime `Supervision` handle), and the Take replay missed that admission's ready→running claim is not a logged transition.\n\nTracked in git-bug: `1ba1eff` `3c6cafb` `e7cdb54` `8051353` `10a51f4` `b8083a8` `1355728` `361a6fd`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}